# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, whether a file is stored with LF or CRLF depends on each
# contributor's core.autocrlf setting. Files committed with CRLF then show up
# as permanently "modified" on machines with autocrlf=true, even when the
# working copy is byte-for-byte identical to what was committed.
#
# text=auto  -> git decides what is text and normalises it to LF in the repo
# eol=lf     -> and checks it out as LF everywhere, regardless of platform
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
